{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"bef89feea24eaf29","name":"card_event_defend_the_empire","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/events/card_event_defend_the_empire","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DEFEND THE NATION","text":"Draw the top non-French card of your deck, then shuffle your deck.","flavorText":"During WWII, faced with German occupation and the collaboration of the Vichy regime, many French citizens took up arms in the shadows to defend their homeland. The emerging resistance networks were initially independent and fragmented. In 1942, General de Gaulle tasked Jean Moulin with unifying these movements under the banner of Free France. Under Moulin's leadership, three major resistance groups of the Southern Zone joined to form the “Armée Secrète” (Secret Army) in September 1942, later consolidating into the “Mouvements Unis de la Résistance” (MUR, United Resistance Movements) in January 1943. Following the creation of the “Conseil National de la Résistance” (National Council of the Resistance) in May 1943 and Moulin's arrest, the MUR and a few Northern Zone groups united as the “Mouvement de Libération Nationale” (MLN, National Liberation Movement) in January 1944. The MLN organized clandestine operations (sabotage, intelligence, underground press) and, after its integration into the Forces Françaises de l'Intérieur (FFI, French Forces of the Interior) in February 1944, coordinated with Allied forces to prepare for Liberation. This unification granted the Resistance military effectiveness, critical to France's role in its own liberation, and political legitimacy, ensuring the nation could determine its postwar future itself. Beyond the fight for freedom, it laid the foundation for France's democratic rebirth.","faction":"France","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_defend_the_empire","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_defend_the_empire_title","SourceString":"DEFEND THE NATION","LocalizedString":"DEFEND THE NATION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_defend_the_empire_text","SourceString":"Draw the top non-French card of your deck, then shuffle your deck.","LocalizedString":"Draw the top non-French card of your deck, then shuffle your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_defend_the_empire_history","SourceString":"During WWII, faced with German occupation and the collaboration of the Vichy regime, many French citizens took up arms in the shadows to defend their homeland. The emerging resistance networks were initially independent and fragmented. In 1942, General de Gaulle tasked Jean Moulin with unifying these movements under the banner of Free France. Under Moulin's leadership, three major resistance groups of the Southern Zone joined to form the “Armée Secrète” (Secret Army) in September 1942, later consolidating into the “Mouvements Unis de la Résistance” (MUR, United Resistance Movements) in January 1943. Following the creation of the “Conseil National de la Résistance” (National Council of the Resistance) in May 1943 and Moulin's arrest, the MUR and a few Northern Zone groups united as the “Mouvement de Libération Nationale” (MLN, National Liberation Movement) in January 1944. The MLN organized clandestine operations (sabotage, intelligence, underground press) and, after its integration into the Forces Françaises de l'Intérieur (FFI, French Forces of the Interior) in February 1944, coordinated with Allied forces to prepare for Liberation. This unification granted the Resistance military effectiveness, critical to France's role in its own liberation, and political legitimacy, ensuring the nation could determine its postwar future itself. Beyond the fight for freedom, it laid the foundation for France's democratic rebirth.","LocalizedString":"During WWII, faced with German occupation and the collaboration of the Vichy regime, many French citizens took up arms in the shadows to defend their homeland. The emerging resistance networks were initially independent and fragmented. In 1942, General de Gaulle tasked Jean Moulin with unifying these movements under the banner of Free France. Under Moulin's leadership, three major resistance groups of the Southern Zone joined to form the “Armée Secrète” (Secret Army) in September 1942, later consolidating into the “Mouvements Unis de la Résistance” (MUR, United Resistance Movements) in January 1943. Following the creation of the “Conseil National de la Résistance” (National Council of the Resistance) in May 1943 and Moulin's arrest, the MUR and a few Northern Zone groups united as the “Mouvement de Libération Nationale” (MLN, National Liberation Movement) in January 1944. The MLN organized clandestine operations (sabotage, intelligence, underground press) and, after its integration into the Forces Françaises de l'Intérieur (FFI, French Forces of the Interior) in February 1944, coordinated with Allied forces to prepare for Liberation. This unification granted the Resistance military effectiveness, critical to France's role in its own liberation, and political legitimacy, ensuring the nation could determine its postwar future itself. Beyond the fight for freedom, it laid the foundation for France's democratic rebirth."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/NavalWarfare/t_mln.t_mln","SubPathString":""},"artist":"French WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DEFEND_THE_NATION.DEFEND_THE_NATION","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":337.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_defend_the_empire_photo","SourceString":"Parade of the Armée Secrète in Bergerac following the city's liberation, 21 August 1944.","LocalizedString":"Parade of the Armée Secrète in Bergerac following the city's liberation, 21 August 1944."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"Image needed to be customized","isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"tmpCard","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"cardFound","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_defend_the_empire","owner":"card_event_defend_the_empire_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_bool_True_if_break_was_hit_Variable","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Not_PreBool_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetDeckByside_deckCardIDs","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_text_Variable","type":"FText","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Get_Item","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Length_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Less_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_BooleanAND_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetCardFromID_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_EnumCompareFaction_Branches","type":"EnumAreTheyEqual","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_SwitchEnum_CmpSuccess","type":"bool","dire